# Road posts: what's moving on the road (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs"), in the post's voice. The crews
# see who lost what, and say it the way their side would.

conv post.bastion.road
for post:bastion
when !hunted:bastion
topic "What's moving on the road?"
prio world
voice bastion

bind horde = news:horde
bind lost = news:lost_by(redhand)
bind truck = supply:truck

node start
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:lost_by(redhand) -> sold
  say? supply:road & bound:truck :: Our supply truck is outbound to {bind:truck} this hour. Don't wave it down and don't walk close to it. The gunner has orders, and the orders don't know your face.
  say? night :: At night? Lights in the fields we can't explain, and engines we can. Mostly the engines: Red Hand lorries running between their tolls with the headlamps off.
  say? fog :: Fog off the low ground. The road could be full of anything for two hundred metres either side of {here}. We assume it is, and so should you.
  say Carts, bikes, people on foot carrying everything they own, the same as every day since the roads shut. Most of them are making for a Haven house. Most of them get there.
  > @back0 Understood, corporal. -> hub

node horde
  say Contact moving near {bind:horde}. A big group, following noise: a shot, an engine, a door banging in the wind. If you're going that way, go quiet, go round, and don't fire unless you have to.
  > @back1 I'll keep clear of {bind:horde}. -> hub

node sold
  say The Red Hand lost {bind:lost}. We watched them leave it through the glasses: fast, and without their lorry. Whatever they tell you at the toll, that wasn't a sale. ~truth:gossip.sold@lost
  > @back2 Good to know. Thanks. -> hub

conv post.redhand.road
for post:redhand
when !hunted:redhand
topic "Anything worth knowing on this road?"
prio world
voice redhand

bind lost = news:lost_by(bastion)
bind truck = news:truck

node start
  jump news:lost_by(bastion) -> withdrew
  jump news:truck -> truck
  say? rain :: Rain. People walk faster in rain and argue less at the lorry. They pay faster too. Best weather we get, honestly.
  say? night :: Nothing that pays. Things in the ditches that bite, and Bastion's lot creeping about with no lights. Different line in the book, both of them.
  say Business. Two carts, a bike and a man with a goat since breakfast. The goat paid. The man's still sat at the bend, thinking about it.
  > @back0 Thanks. I'll mind the bend. -> hub

node withdrew
  say Bastion left {bind:lost}. At a run. We watched from the ridge. Withdrew, they'll call it on their net. Withdrew at a sprint, with the kettle still on. ~truth:gossip.withdrew@lost
  > @back1 I'll remember that. -> hub

node truck
  say A truck bound for {bind:truck} never got there. Not one of ours: ours get there, that's the whole point of paying us. Somebody's shelves are empty tonight, and our prices just went up.
  > @back2 Not your truck. Got it. -> hub
